## THE SAFEHOUSE

The address Vera provided led to an abandoned factory—industrial district, nondescript, easy to miss.

Dax parked in the vehicle bay. Killed the engine.

"Looks clear," he said. Pause. "Too clear."

Silas drew his pistol. "Could be trap."

Kai stepped out. Scanned the perimeter. No movement. No heat signatures. But instinct screamed: *This is wrong.*

They entered through a side door—rusted hinges groaning, darkness beyond.

Inside: Not abandoned.

Furnished. Cots lined the walls. Supply crates stacked neatly. Weapons cache in the corner. Intel boards covered in maps, photos, notes.

Someone had prepared this.

The crew spread out.

Dax checked the medical supplies: "This is Stitch-level. Professional field kit."

Silas examined the ammunition: "Military grade. Atlas markings."

Kai approached the intel board.

Maps of Ashen Reach—districts marked, council chambers highlighted, arena locations circled. The Scar's entrance points noted. Facility ruins flagged.

One location circled in red ink: **"WHERE IT STARTED"**

A note pinned to the map—handwriting Kai recognized immediately.

*"Welcome home, brother."*

His blood went cold.

"Kieran set this up," he said.

Dax appeared at his shoulder. "How do you know?"

Kai held up the note.

Dax read it. "Shit."

"We're in his territory," Silas said from across the room. "He's watching. Probably always has been."

"Question is," Kai said quietly, "why help us get here just to watch us?"

No answer.

They worked in silence—Dax rigging motion sensors on the perimeter, Silas checking weapons, Kai studying Kieran's maps.

His brother's handwriting. His notes. His strategy.

Kieran had been planning this. Waiting for Kai to come back.

But for what? Revenge? Reunion? Something worse?

Kai touched the pendant again. Felt its weight.

Two brothers. Both ghosts. One waiting, one arriving.

What happened when ghosts collided?

